PRP-RE1: Rules Engine Refactor - Query-Based Regulatory Discovery
Started: 2025-08-31
Branch: rules-engine-refactor
Status: IN PROGRESS

Objective: Transform hardcoded Marrickville R2-only setback calculator into universal 
Inner West regulatory engine that discovers rules dynamically via LightRAG/AutoSchemaKG queries.

Key Goals:
- Support ANY zone (R1/R2/R3/R4/B1/B2/IN1/etc.)
- Support ANY development type (dwelling/multi/commercial/industrial)
- Query existing processed data instead of hardcoding regulatory paths
- Extract zone→section relationships from knowledge graph
- Handle edge cases with confidence scoring

Phase 1 Deliverables:
- services/universal_regulatory_engine.py
- services/dynamic_dcp_resolver.py
- services/regulatory_relationship_extractor.py
- services/setback_value_extractor.py
- services/confidence_scorer.py

Current Focus: Setting up query-based discovery infrastructure to replace hardcoded rules.